{"tool_name":"spaced_radiology","contents":["oeb","bioschemas","biotools"],"fetched_metadata":{"biotools":{"id":"Spaced_Radiology","home":"http://www.spacedradiology.com/","license":"Unlicense","summary":"Encouraging durable memory using spaced testing in pediatric radiology.","addition_date":"2019-08-09T13:14:44Z","last_update_date":"2020-06-16T10:55:26Z","tool_type":["Web application"],"accessibility":"Restricted access","biotools_curie":"biotools:Spaced_Radiology","cost":"Free of charge (with restrictions)","credit":[{"email":"cara.morin@stjude.org","name":"Cara E. Morin","orcidid":"https://orcid.org/0000-0003-1953-4486","typeEntity":"Person","typeRole":["Primary contact"]},{"email":"mishaherscu@gmail.com","typeRole":["Primary contact"]}],"documentation":[{"type":["General"],"url":"http://www.spacedradiology.com/#/about"}],"edit_permission":{"type":"private"},"maturity":"Mature","name":"Spaced Radiology","operating_system":["Linux","Mac","Windows"],"owner":"hans","publication":[{"doi":"10.1007/S00247-019-04415-3","metadata":{"abstract":"\u00a9 2019, The Author(s).Applied memory research in the field of cognitive and educational psychology has generated a large body of data to support the use of spacing and testing to promote long-term or durable memory. Despite the consensus of this scientific community, most learners, including radiology residents, do not utilize these tools for learning new information. We present a discussion of these parallel and synergistic learning techniques and their incorporation into a software platform, called Spaced Radiology, which we created for teaching radiology residents. Specifically, this software uses these evidence-based strategies to teach pediatric radiology through a flashcard deck system.","authors":[{"name":"Hostetter J.M."},{"name":"Jeudy J."},{"name":"Kim J.S."},{"name":"Kim W.G."},{"name":"McCabe J.A."},{"name":"Merrow A.C."},{"name":"Morin C.E."},{"name":"Ropp A.M."},{"name":"Shet N.S."},{"name":"Sidhu A.S."}],"citat